label ending:
    scene cafe with fade
    if flags.plan_cafe:
        narrator "The Spare Room opens three evenings a week. Hana has time to illustrate; maintenance is paid work. June sends postcards instead of emergency instructions."
    else:
        narrator "The original café closes. Once a month, the Spare Room supper club fills the community hall. June's recipe tin travels from kitchen to kitchen. The place mattered; the people were never only its furniture."
    if rel.hana.status == "closed" or rel.hana.repair:
        narrator "Your connection with Hana ends with distance. The story does not turn an unresolved boundary into forgiveness."
    elif rel.hana.status == "exclusive":
        narrator "Hana saves you a seat at breakfast, then leaves for her illustration deadline. That evening she returns with a story she has been saving for you, a kiss hello, and an invitation to cuddle on the window bench."
        narrator "You have made room for two lives, not one person doing all the caring."
    elif (rel.hana.status == "exploring" or rel.hana.status == "shared") and not rel.hana.repair:
        narrator "You and Hana have another date planned. Neither pretends that a beginning is a guarantee; both want to see what comes next."
    elif rel.hana.status == "friend" or (rel.hana.visits >= 2 and rel.hana.trust >= 3):
        narrator "Your friendship with Hana continues through a seat on her actual break. It is chosen company, not a consolation prize."
    if rel.mira.status == "closed" or rel.mira.repair:
        narrator "Your connection with Mira ends with distance. The story does not turn an unresolved boundary into forgiveness."
    elif rel.mira.status == "exclusive":
        narrator "Wednesday dinner becomes a ritual, followed by a film, a shared blanket, and kisses she no longer disguises as a dare. Some evenings Mira is hilarious; some she is tired from class. Both versions get an invitation."
        narrator "One night she says she missed you and lets the sentence end there."
    elif (rel.mira.status == "exploring" or rel.mira.status == "shared") and not rel.mira.repair:
        narrator "You and Mira have another date planned. Neither pretends that a beginning is a guarantee; both want to see what comes next."
    elif rel.mira.status == "friend" or (rel.mira.visits >= 2 and rel.mira.trust >= 3):
        narrator "Your friendship with Mira continues through a film night without romantic ambiguity. It is chosen company, not a consolation prize."
    if rel.leila.status == "closed" or rel.leila.repair:
        narrator "Your connection with Leila ends with distance. The story does not turn an unresolved boundary into forgiveness."
    elif rel.leila.status == "exclusive":
        narrator "A goodbye kiss and a long embrace become the first of many reunions to look forward to. The first call starts with a blurry ceiling and an argument about where to put the phone. You arrange a visit you can both afford."
        narrator "Distance is real, and so is the next conversation."
    elif (rel.leila.status == "exploring" or rel.leila.status == "shared") and not rel.leila.repair:
        narrator "You and Leila have another date planned. Neither pretends that a beginning is a guarantee; both want to see what comes next."
    elif rel.leila.status == "friend" or (rel.leila.visits >= 2 and rel.leila.trust >= 3):
        narrator "Your friendship with Leila continues through a postcard and a call from the new city. It is chosen company, not a consolation prize."
    if rel.tessa.status == "closed" or rel.tessa.repair:
        narrator "Your connection with Tessa ends with distance. The story does not turn an unresolved boundary into forgiveness."
    elif rel.tessa.status == "exclusive":
        narrator "Tessa leaves a shelf unfinished to meet you. You both know it can wait. Her kiss hello is followed by an invitation to curl up together on the sofa, with no task to justify staying."
        narrator "She asks for help when she needs it and company when she wants it; you learn to do the same."
    elif (rel.tessa.status == "exploring" or rel.tessa.status == "shared") and not rel.tessa.repair:
        narrator "You and Tessa have another date planned. Neither pretends that a beginning is a guarantee; both want to see what comes next."
    elif rel.tessa.status == "friend" or (rel.tessa.visits >= 2 and rel.tessa.trust >= 3):
        narrator "Your friendship with Tessa continues through breakfast without anything needing repairs. It is chosen company, not a consolation prize."
    if flags.everyone_agreed and rel.hana.status == "shared" and not rel.hana.repair and rel.mira.status == "shared" and not rel.mira.repair and rel.leila.status == "shared" and not rel.leila.repair and rel.tessa.status == "shared" and not rel.tessa.repair:
        narrator "The five of you build a relationship with room for individual dates and shared evenings."
        narrator "Hana keeps a breakfast morning with you; Mira claims a film night by asking, not competing; Leila joins from the residency and plans her next visit; Tessa protects time when nobody needs to be useful."
        narrator "You speak about jealousy before it hardens into resentment, and nobody has to surrender her own life to stay loved. On the first reunion weekend, the sofa proves much too small."
        narrator "Tessa fetches another blanket, Hana settles close, Mira asks for her goodnight kiss, and Leila finally puts her phone away. There are kisses, warm embraces, and a laughing negotiation over whose cold feet are whose."
        narrator "Each person is here because she chose to be. Tomorrow still contains separate plans; tonight contains all five of you."
    if not (flags.everyone_agreed and rel.hana.status == "shared" and not rel.hana.repair and rel.mira.status == "shared" and not rel.mira.repair and rel.leila.status == "shared" and not rel.leila.repair and rel.tessa.status == "shared" and not rel.tessa.repair) and rel.hana.status != "exclusive" and rel.mira.status != "exclusive" and rel.leila.status != "exclusive" and rel.tessa.status != "exclusive":
        narrator "You leave this summer without needing a relationship label to prove it mattered. There are invitations you can accept, and room to make your own life."
    narrator "The light is on. What happens next Tuesday is yours to choose."
    end "The Light We Leave On"
